{title: Holy God, We Praise Thy Name}
{artist: Ignaz Franz, tr. Clarence A. Walworth / Grosser Gott (1774)}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: F}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{score: holy-god-we-praise-thy-name.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Holy_God_We_Praise_Thy_Name-Te_Deum-Hursley)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Holy God, we [C7]praise Thy [F]name;
[F]Lord of all, we bow be[C]fore Thee!
[F]All on earth Thy [C7]scepter [F]claim,
[F]All in Heaven above a[C]dore Thee;
[C]Infin[Gm]ite [C]Thy [F]vast do[C]main,
[Bb]Ever[C7]last[Dm]ing [Bb]is [C7]Thy [F]reign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Hark! the loud ce[C7]lestial [F]hymn
[F]Angel choirs above are [C]raising,
[F]Cherubim and [C7]sera[F]phim,
[F]In unceasing chorus [C]praising;
[C]Fill the [Gm]heavens [C]with [F]sweet ac[C]cord:
[Bb]Holy, [C7]ho[Dm]ly, [Bb]ho[C7]ly, [F]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Lo! the apost[C7]olic [F]train
[F]Join the sacred name to [C]hallow;
[F]Prophets swell the [C7]loud re[F]frain,
[F]And the white robed martyrs [C]follow;
[C]And from [Gm]morn [C]to [F]set of [C]sun,
[Bb]Through the [C7]Church [Dm]the [Bb]song [C7]goes [F]on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Holy Father, [C7]Holy [F]Son,
[F]Holy Spirit, Three we [C]name Thee;
[F]While in essence [C7]only [F]One,
[F]Undivided God we [C]claim Thee;
[C]And a[Gm]dor[C]ing [F]bend the [C]knee,
[Bb]While we [C7]own [Dm]the [Bb]my[C7]ster[F]y.
{end_of_verse}
